THOUGHT: The remaining NullAway errors say both constructors don’t initialize modelChannel. Since modelChannel is always set in allocateChannels() before use, the simplest fix is to initialize it to a safe dummy value in the field declaration using a minimal anonymous ObjectChannel implementation, avoiding null while not depending on ParallelArray’s enclosing instance.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i 's/^  public Array<Model> models;
-  ObjectChannel<ModelInstance> modelChannel;/  public Array<Model> models;
+  ObjectChannel<ModelInstance> modelChannel = new ObjectChannel<ModelInstance>(ModelInstance.class) {
+    @Override
+    public void add(int index, int count) {}
+
+    @Override
+    public void remove(int index, int count) {}
+  };
/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g3d/particles/influencers/ModelInfluencer.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && (grep -n "ModelInfluencer.java" new_build_output.log || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log)
```

